# SDLC How-To

Use the `how-to` skill when a user asks how to use `umo-sdlc`, how to navigate a
repo, where docs/issues/dependencies live, how to follow SDLC, SDD, or TDD, how
to adapt a repo to the plugin, why agents are not following it, or whether a
repo is healthy for docs/planning/Beads workflows.

## Scope

The how-to skill is the broad orientation and diagnostics entry point. It may
explain, inspect, report, route to specific skills, and apply safe local fixes.
It delegates deep document work to `docs` and deep Beads planning work to
`planning`.

## Safe Defaults

- Default to observe/report mode.
- Keep repo `AGENTS.md` files as thin steering and binding layers.
- Do not duplicate full SDLC lifecycle, Beads label taxonomy, or planning
  templates into local `AGENTS.md`.
- Route future plugin capabilities through the most specific available skill or
  rule instead of expanding local steering.
- Require explicit approval before bulk `AGENTS.md` edits, docs moves,
  proposal/ADR status changes, Beads initialization, enforcement changes, or
  plugin manifest changes.

## Required Skill

For how-to guidance, service navigation, adoption checks, repository health
diagnostics, safe autofixes, and report shape, load:

`plugins/umo-sdlc/skills/how-to/SKILL.md`
